  "caption": "Quinn's December calendar is full, sleep has been pushed to next year, and the old back pain is back for the season, with shoulders up near the ears.\n\nStress can turn up pain sensitivity. Short sleep lowers pain tolerance, tension adds load to the neck and shoulders, A familiar flare in a hard season often reflects a sensitive system rather than new damage. The pain is real.\n\nWhat often helps: keep moving at a lighter level, protect your sleep, downshift on purpose with slow breathing or a short walk outside, and combine a few approaches.\n\nNew pain in new places, night pain, numbness, weakness or fever are worth getting assessed. If stress or low mood is weighing heavily, talk to your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
